  message: "F5 Rust slice merged dev 7d015b818b — the gate ratchet's FIRST DOUBLE strip (both rust holes in one PR). rust.py now emits: (a) kind='field' per NAMED struct field (Struct::field, Rust :: member convention; node-id segment collapses ::->. like impl methods; tuple structs skipped), and (b) kind='variable' per module-level const_item/static_item (new _is_rust_module_level_const guard: top-level + mod-level only; excludes fn-body locals and impl/trait-associated consts). Both canonical make_typed_stable_id, type as signature, pub->is_exported. Strips (rust, emits_field) AND (rust, emits_variable) -> hard locks (86 passed / 11 xfailed). Also scoped test_rust_scip_stable_id's parity collector to function/method (the SCIP function-parity helper does not cover the new field/const spans — caught by the full affected suite, fixed).\n\nGATE HOLES REMAINING (only 2 languages left): emits_field = python (class attributes), swift; emits_variable = swift. Done: JS/TS (both kinds), Java/Go/C# (field), Rust (field + variable). NEXT candidates: Swift (double strip — class properties + top-level let/var) or Python (class-attribute field emission — its only gap, since python already emits module vars)."  # 4fad
