- op: discuss  # 774d
  at: '2026-07-04T14:50:33Z'  # 774d
  by: agent  # 774d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 774d
  clock: 15  # 774d
  nonce: 774d  # 774d
  message: "Scala tail-language slice LANDED — PR merged, dev f1782af4a7 (advances WI-jusus by one non-gated tail language; item STAYS todo_hard — the tail dart/haskell/ocaml/... continues). scala.py now emits kind=field for val/var in a named class/object/trait/enum/given body and kind=variable for top-level val/var (was 0 field/0 variable), mirroring the kotlin slice via _scala_property_scope.\n\nAdversarial review (3 refuters) returned NO_GO-as-written -> fixed to GO. It confirmed the swift-INV-lanaz/go-INV-sidab local-leak class was LIVE for scala: case-body vals (partial-function literals / match / try-catch initializing a field or top-level val, immediate parent case_clause) and Scala-3 braceless indented_block leaked as fields/variables. FIXED: _SCALA_LOCAL_SCOPE_TYPES now includes case_clause + indented_block. Also MAJOR-fixed: enum_body + given with_template_body now classify as fields (were wrongly bare top-level variables); and a call-graph-corruption vector (a bare call resolving to a same-short-name field via the resolver suffix index / short-name registration) closed by (a) not registering field/variable short names in symbol_by_name (mirrors commit 67b2e14788) and (b) the resolver call-resolution refusing a field/variable target. Documented fails-safe deferrals (miss, never wrong): primary-ctor val params, multi-name bindings, package objects.\n\n20 dedicated tests (incl. 7 review-fix regressions: partial-fn/match/try-catch case-local, indented_block, enum field, given field, call-graph integrity) + comprehensive re-probe (nested class owner=Inner, anon-given skip, for/while locals, all clean). 100% cov; smart-test 3874 passed. awaits_bakeoff_validation stays (blast-radius scala emission change)."  # 774d
- op: discuss  # 2a66
  at: '2026-07-05T21:25:45Z'  # 2a66
  by: agent  # 2a66
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a66
  clock: 16  # 2a66
  nonce: 2a66  # 2a66
  message: "Dart tail-language slice LANDED — PR #440 merged, dev 9dbc52da37 (advances WI-jusus by one non-gated tail language; item STAYS todo_hard — the haskell/ocaml/... tail continues). dart.py now emits kind=field for class/mixin/extension/enum-body value declarations and kind=variable for top-level declarations (was 0/0), matching the initialized_identifier_list (var/typed) and static_final_declaration_list (const/static/final-inferred) tree-sitter nodes, classified by immediate structural context (declaration under class_body/extension_body/enum_body -> field owner=enclosing type; direct child of program -> variable).\n\nSTRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE from the kotlin/scala/swift slices: Dart fn/method/for/lambda/if-block LOCALS use a DISTINCT node type (local_variable_declaration -> initialized_variable_definition) and can NEVER match the field/variable nodes, so the swift-INV-lanaz / go-INV-sidab local-leak class is structurally impossible here (verified by AST probe across method/for/lambda/if/while/try/switch bodies) — no scope-walk needed, unlike kotlin/scala.\n\nAdversarial review (2 refuters, both NO-GO-as-written -> GO; full analysis ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/design_analyses/wi-jusus-dart-field-variable-design_07052026.md). Caught TWO real defects an inline fix would have shipped: (1) call-graph registry-CLOBBER — a bare-named top-level variable registers under the SAME flat key as a same-named function, so a kind-gate at the edge sites would only turn the false-positive into a false-NEGATIVE (drop the real function call); FIXED structurally by overriding DartAnalyzer.register_symbol to skip field/variable kinds (never call/instantiate targets), a single chokepoint that closes false-positive + suffix-shadow false-negative + clobber at once and touches no edge site; symbols still reach output/search/centrality since base.py builds all_symbols from analysis.symbols independently of the resolution registry. (2) Dart-3 record/list/map PATTERN-DECLARATION mis-parse — this grammar has no pattern support, so 'var (a,b)=pair;' salvages the RHS as a spurious initialized_identifier_list; guarded by skipping any value list with an ERROR preceding sibling (fails-safe; also drops the rare abstract/external field the grammar mis-parses, a documented deferral).\n\nBehavioral evidence (live hypergumbo analyze): a file with 'const int maxDelay', 'var currentItems', 'class Counter { int count; final String _label; void tick(){ var local; } }' -> fields Counter.count/Counter._label + variables maxDelay/currentItems, method-local 'local' EXCLUDED. 11 dedicated tests (incl. local-exclusion, getter/setter-not-field, destructuring guard, variable-does-not-clobber-function-resolution, field-not-a-call-target, instantiation-edges-preserved) + full dart suite (63) + cross-package core dart tests (729) green. 100% isolation coverage on dart.py. awaits_bakeoff_validation stays (blast-radius emission change across the Dart corpus — a DEEP cohort should confirm right-reason field/variable materialization, locals excluded, like the validated kotlin/scala slices)."  # 2a66
