  message: "Solidity tail-language slice LANDED — PR #441 merged, dev a52887c7e7 (advances WI-jusus by another non-gated tail language; item STAYS todo_hard — the haskell/ocaml/... tail continues). solidity.py now emits kind=field for contract STATE VARIABLES (the security-critical persistent storage: taint source/sink, io-boundary anchor, what functions read/write) and struct members, and kind=variable for file-level constants (was 0/0). Three tree-sitter nodes: state_variable_declaration under contract_body -> field (owner=enclosing contract/interface/library, visibility from the visibility child, public->is_exported); struct_member -> field (owner=enclosing struct); constant_variable_declaration directly under source_file -> variable (contract-level constants parse as state_variable_declaration and route through the field path).\n\nSTRUCTURAL: like dart (and unlike kotlin/scala/swift), Solidity fn/modifier/ctor/loop/unchecked/assembly LOCALS use a DISTINCT node type (variable_declaration inside variable_declaration_statement) and can NEVER match the three emitted nodes, so the swift-INV-lanaz/go-INV-sidab local-leak class is structurally impossible — no scope-walk needed. Adversarially confirmed the locals-never-leak guarantee holds even under parse-error recovery.\n\nCall-graph integrity closed at one chokepoint (mirrors the dart slice): SolidityAnalyzer.register_symbol skips field/variable AND add_value_symbol writes only to analysis.symbols (never symbol_by_name), so a state variable — never a call target (a public state var's auto getter is a synthesized function, not this symbol) — can neither clobber a same-named function's flat registry key nor be a suffix-matched spurious calls target.\n\nAdversarial review (1 refuter, 7 vectors) returned GO with no defects: end-to-end proof that a coexisting field Store.value + function Store.value resolve the call to the FUNCTION with 0 spurious edges; confirmed no MISS for library/interface/abstract-contract constants (they route through the field path); name extraction reads the direct identifier child (never the type_name) for array/mapping/user-defined-type declarations. 6 dedicated tests + full solidity suite (66) + cross-package core solidity tests (967) green. 100% isolation coverage on solidity.py. Behavioral (live analyze): a Vault contract -> Vault.owner/balances/totalDeposits + Deposit.amount/timestamp fields + VERSION variable, owner exported/balances not, local amt excluded. awaits_bakeoff_validation stays (blast-radius emission change across the Solidity corpus)."  # 4975
- op: discuss  # 43dc
