  nonce: 43dc  # 43dc
  message: "Julia struct-field slice LANDED — PR #442 merged, dev 4fcd9fbd16 (advances WI-jusus by another non-gated tail language; item STAYS todo_hard). julia.py now emits kind=field for struct members (was: struct type only, 0 fields). A typed_expression (x::Float64) -> field with the parametric-aware type as signature; a bare identifier -> untyped field. Owner = struct name; underscore -> not is_exported.\n\nGRAMMAR-DIVERGENCE TRAP (the kotlin lesson, caught by TDD): the analyzer's bundled tree_sitter_julia grammar lists struct members as DIRECT children of struct_definition, while tree_sitter_language_pack wraps them in a . My initial extraction used find_child_by_type(node,'block') (langpack shape) -> returned None under the bundled grammar -> 0 fields, but the RED tests (which run analyze_julia = bundled grammar) caught it. Fixed to handle both: members = block.children if block else node.children. A SECOND divergence: Julia-1.8  struct fields parse as an ERROR node under the bundled grammar (predates the feature) -> deferred fails-safe (miss, never emit wrong); sibling non-const fields still emit.\n\nInner constructors (Widget(s)=new(s), an assignment) and function-body locals (distinct nodes) never leak. Call-graph integrity via the same chokepoint as dart/solidity: JuliaAnalyzer.register_symbol skips field + emitter writes only to analysis.symbols (never symbol_by_name), so a field can't clobber/shadow a same-named function.\n\nModule-level  is ALREADY emitted (kind='const'); non-const module globals need scope discrimination (bare assignment appears at module level AND inside functions) and are a deferred follow-up — this slice is struct-fields only.\n\n7 dedicated tests (incl. the const-field deferral + grammar-both-shapes) + full julia suite (35) green. 100% isolation coverage on julia.py. Behavioral (live analyze): struct Circle <: Shape {radius::Float64, center::Vector{Float64}, label} + inner ctor -> Circle.radius/center/label (ctor excluded, parametric type captured); mutable Counter {count::Int, _internal::Bool} -> count exported, _internal not; function-local excluded. awaits_bakeoff_validation stays."  # 43dc
